DESCRIPTION:It's Always the End of the World (1h 39min)\n\nMax and Charlott
 e take a trip to a cabin once owned by Charlotte’s now deceased uncle. Bur
 ied in the bushes outside of the cabin\, Max finds an old trunk stuffed wi
 th documents\, audio cassettes and VHS tapes. The trunk’s contents point t
 owards a half century of murder\, secrets and abuse - Max slowly becomes o
 bsessed as he grows closer and closer to learning the truth about the myst
 ery\, Britain’s past and the nature of life itself.\n\nStarring: Jacob Mel
 lers\, Robyn Faye\n\nFilm release at WTW Cinemas Wadebridge\nBook tickets:
